From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:53:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(approval): a subagent's review reads the root chat live

Smart approval (provenance) judged a subagent against the in-memory message list of the root AIAgent object it held by weakref, which is set only while that object runs tools. A message the user wrote in the root chat after the spawn was missed when the cached root agent was rebuilt or evicted, or had not run a tool since, so the subagent saw only the parent's relayed claim. When the weakref died, the subagent's own transcript (the parent's goal and steers) was read as the user's words.

A subagent now records the root chat's session id at spawn (a nested subagent inherits its parent's), and each review reads the root transcript from the session store at the tip of its compression chain, adding rows of the root's running turn not yet stored. The parent's goal and steers stay labeled as not the user. A subagent whose root chat can be read neither from the store nor from a live root agent gets an unsure verdict, which asks the user.
